Description: libmount: reuse existing act fd in mnt_update_start on ro retry
 When mnt_context_mount() retries a failed mount as read-only,
 mnt_context_prepare_update() calls mnt_update_start() a second time.
 Without checking whether act_fd is already open, the old fd is
 overwritten and leaked, and its LOCK_SH prevents mnt_update_end() from
 unlinking the act file. Guard mnt_update_start() with an act_fd >= 0
 check to reuse the existing fd instead of opening a new one.
Author: wangrong <wangrong@uniontech.com>
Last-Update: 2026-08-20
---

--- a/libmount/src/tab_update.c
+++ b/libmount/src/tab_update.c
@@ -1056,6 +1056,11 @@
 	    asprintf(&upd->act_filename, "%s.act", upd->filename) <= 0)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	if (upd->act_fd >= 0) {
+		DBG(UPDATE, ul_debugobj(upd, "reusing existing act file"));
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/* Use exclusive lock to avoid some other proces will remove the the
 	 * file before it's marked as used by LOCK_SH (below) */
 	rc = update_init_lock(upd, NULL);
